{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For also.</b> Every time in the language of the Sacred, it is joined to masculine plural forms, and it is always feminine gender, except for only this one instance of Samson, and the sense is: do not be concerned about the words of those who despise and curse, for you already know that you too have cursed others — whether with your mouth or in your thoughts."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:13.401186608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}